{
  "id": "Compound::DB00977 - Gene::6462",
  "verbalization": "Ethinyl Estradiol is implicated in the binding of Shbg through a shared pathway involving Etonogestrel, a therapeutic steroid hormone. The evidence suggests that Ethinyl Estradiol causes various adverse effects, all of which are mediated by Etonogestrel, which in turn binds to Shbg. This indicates a potential functional link between Ethinyl Estradiol and Shbg, possibly through the influence of Etonogestrel. The lowest common ancestors of Ethinyl Estradiol and Etonogestrel are both classified under the broader category of therapeutic steroid hormones and 17-hydroxy steroids, suggesting a common biological context. The consistent presence of Etonogestrel as a mediator in multiple pathways involving Shbg implies that Ethinyl Estradiol may exert its effects via Etonogestrel, which then interacts with Shbg. This integrated explanation highlights the role of Etonogestrel as a critical intermediary in the relationship between Ethinyl Estradiol and Shbg.",
